<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Silver&nbsp;Spoilers</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>O5-4 claims Edwin Hallewell died in 1921. The initial picture was taken in 1922. The Foundation is lying.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>I was inspired to write this when researching neutron stars. <em>It is currently theorized that heavy elements such as platinum, uranium and gold are created when two neutron stars collide. This celestial collision will cause an explosion, tearing them apart, and scattering their metals throughout the universe.</em></p>
<p>Kosser Valley, Feldspar, and all other locations in this article are fictional. Except Colorado, I think. Image sources are <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Iridium_%C3%A9s_Ozmium_ampull%C3%A1zva.jpg">here</a>, <a href="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1a/Interior_view_of_a_mine_%28named_Bagdad_Mine%3F%29_belonging_to_the_Rochester_Gold_Mining_Co.%2C_Ludlow%2C_California%2C_ca.1900_%28CHS-5230%29.jpg">here</a>, <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Familiefoto_Regout-Kersten,_ca_1865.jpg">and here.</a> All under the Creative Commons Attribution-Share Alike 3.0 Unported license.</p>
<p>Thanks to:<br />
