<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>U.S. Legal system</p>
</blockquote>
<p>legal</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Naturally occurring radiation or hazardous chemicals in the area.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Personally I would remove &quot;in the area&quot; since it's a footnote, but it's a preference thing.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>She's got my husbands eyes</p>
</blockquote>
<p>husband's</p>
<blockquote>
<p>She's only 5 years old.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Since this is a transcript of spoken word, I would use &quot;five&quot;.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Maddie had her uncles old radio.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>uncle's</p>
<blockquote>
<p>We were all just a bunch of miners daughters</p>
</blockquote>
<p>miner's</p>
<blockquote>
<p>with the butchers son</p>
</blockquote>
<p>butcher's</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Mr. Hallewell brought in some city-boy tycoons son</p>
</blockquote>
<p>tycoon's</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I saw it's eyes.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>its</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Simultaneous exposure was required to form SCP-4938-1 tumorous growths.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Should be &quot;is required&quot; to match the tense.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The Department of Finance has been tasked with regulating the export of Gold</p>
</blockquote>
<p>gold</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>I also like these stories showing areas where the Foundation exploits the anomalous to make money and fund their operations. All those resources have to come from somewhere&#8230;</p>

