			<div class="content" id="post-content-4321519">
									

<p>I feel like there are parts of the interview that are formatted &quot;oddly&quot; (ellipsis before a phrase or as a method to designate pauses always bugs me), and it came precariously close at several points to reading more like a novel than an article.</p>
<p><em>That being said</em>, I was genuinely surprised by this. The dialogue reads like a story, but it's quite a good one; the writing is clean and compelling, and the ending is deeply satisfying. A very, very easy upvote.</p>

