			<div class="content" id="post-content-4321550">
									

<p>Thanks so much for the read Hippo! Ellipses are ranked just under &quot;s vs 's&quot; in my hurdles as a writer. I'm working to improve within this format.</p>
<p>You're also right that this article is essentially a short-story sandwich, with the article as the bread. I experimented a bit trying to break up Mrs. Walsh's dialogue, intersecting it with the researcher's observations or scoring it with article elements, but it all felt like padding more than pacing. I didn't want to waste the readers time. In the end, I settled on making it just an old woman telling one story, and the Foundation telling another.</p>

